From 56a97a26b43770295da6199c3c42a2206904d09a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wu <wuc8974@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:28:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(device-identity): wire env-var keyring into
 loadOrCreateDeviceIdentity

Closes the M5 fail-OPEN gap. Previously, runtime callers (gateway,
push-apns, heartbeat) called loadOrCreateDeviceIdentity without a
keyring, so the ML-DSA-65 private key was stored in plaintext in
the mldsa_private_key_pem column. Anyone with read access to
state/openclaw.sqlite could recover the long-term identity key.

This commit auto-wires an inline SyncWrappingKeyProvider from
OPENCLAW_PQC_WRAP_KEY[_ID] env vars:

  OPENCLAW_PQC_WRAP_KEY     # 32-byte base64url (required to enable wrap)
  OPENCLAW_PQC_WRAP_KEY_ID  # logical keyId (default "env-default")

Behavior:
  - Both vars set: device identity is wrapped at rest, keyId is
    the user-friendly value from OPENCLAW_PQC_WRAP_KEY_ID.
  - Neither var set: plaintext fallback (with a loud stderr
    warning on first device-identity creation).
  - One var set, the other missing: the missing one defaults
    (wrap key required, keyId defaults to "env-default").
  - Malformed wrap key: throws on startup with a clear error.

Verification:
  - 5 new invariants in src/infra/device-identity-wrap-env.test.ts
  - All 16 wrap-related tests pass (5 new + 11 existing M5)
  - `pnpm build` 4m 14s end-to-end
  - Runtime check: gateway boot with env vars now produces a row
    where mldsa_private_key_wrapped is non-null BLOB and
    mldsa_private_key_pem is null (the M5 mutual-exclusion guarantee)

No changes to M1-M11 PQC crypto code; this is a runtime wiring
fix. The M5 device-identity-store API (wrappingKeyProvider
parameter) is unchanged.
